# Project delivery core

## Stack (active pack)

The `Pack` row in `docs/agents-v0/project-profile.md` is the backend: `java`, `dotnet`, `node`, `python`, or `go`. Versions, layers, auth, migrations, and verify commands are in `.agents-v0/packs/<pack>/PACK.md`. `/v0-architecture` records `Pack:` on the pattern ADR and runs `sh .agents-v0/scripts/activate-stack-pack.sh`. Any other stack stops before `/v0-plan`. `/v0-onboard` records the pack already on disk and does not replace it. P0-A uses `java`. The UI is React 19, TypeScript 5.9, Vite 7; SvelteKit only when the repo already uses it. OpenAPI 3.0 uses `/api/v1/`. Events and cache only when the ADR justifies them. The directory table below is the java layout; another pack uses the layout in its `PACK.md`.

## Directory profiles

Greenfield repos use one profile. Record it under **Layout** in `docs/agents-v0/project-profile.md` (`Profile`, `Backend root`, `Frontend root`, `BFF root`, `Service roots`). A filled Profile or root row wins. `/v0-onboard` records the tree it finds and does not move source. When rows are still placeholders, match the files on disk.

| Profile | When | Code roots |
|---------|------|------------|
| `service` | Pack `java` | `app/backend/`: `src/main/java`, `src/main/resources/db/migration`, `src/test/java`. A BFF-only repo uses `app/bff/` instead of `app/backend/`. Other packs use the layout in their PACK.md |
| `ui` | React default; SvelteKit only if already used | `app/frontend/`. React: `src/pages/`, `src/features/`, `src/components/{layout,common}`, `src/services/api`, `src/store/slices`. Existing SvelteKit: `src/routes/`, `src/lib/` |
| `app` | Service and UI in one repo | `app/backend/` and `app/frontend/` (same trees as `service` and `ui`). Add `app/bff/` only when a BFF is in scope |

The repo root holds `docs/`, `ci/`, and `openapi/`. No root `src/`, `pom.xml`, or `package.json`. `/v0-onboard` may record `.` when a legacy repo already has source at the root.

**Several services in one repo.** List them in `Service roots` (comma-separated, relative: `app/services/order, app/services/inventory`) instead of one `Backend root`; `app/services/*/` JVM modules are also auto-detected. Each root is its own Maven module with its own database, built and scanned by CI (`ci/resolve-layout.sh` prints `SERVICE_ROOTS`) and owns one catalog, `openapi/<service>-v1.yaml` (`<service>` = last segment of the root). The requirements artifact records `Service root:`. A story that touches two services is two stories plus an integration story (`program-planning`). Maven config paths: `maven/quality-plugins.xml`. CI does not cross git repositories; list other repos in `docs/agents-v0/workspace.manifest.json`.

Pack `java` uses packages `api`, `service`, `repository`, and `domain`. Other packs use the layout in their PACK.md. New OpenAPI contracts default to `openapi/api-v1.yaml`. That file is the org catalog. Design drafts the feature fragment at `docs/agents-v0/design/<feature>/openapi.yaml`. Build merges the approved fragment into the catalog before implementation (`workflow-orchestration.mdc`). Verify commands are the profile rows, run inside the code root. CI reads the Layout table via `ci/resolve-layout.sh`.

## Cross-cutting (all services)

- **Correlation ID:** propagate on every request (header + MDC/logs); return on responses when applicable.
- **Distributed tracing:** W3C Trace Context (`traceparent`, `tracestate` if used); prefer **OpenTelemetry** aligned with platform (Jaeger, Tempo, Datadog, etc.).
- **Structured logging:** JSON or stable key–value fields; include `traceId` / `spanId` when OTel populates MDC.
- **Metrics:** Prometheus (or platform equivalent); RED-style signals (rate, errors, duration) for HTTP and critical dependencies.
- **Auth:** JWT for users; S2S via `X-API-Key` or service Bearer per repo. Never log tokens or secrets.
- **Resilience:** circuit breaker, retry with backoff, timeouts on outbound HTTP; idempotent event consumers.
- **Health:** `/health` (and `/ready` / `/live` if the project uses them).

## API envelopes (default)

| Type | Shape |
|------|------|
| Success | `{ success, data, metadata }` — lists: `page`, `limit`, `total`, `totalPages` |
| Error | `{ success: false, error: { code, message, details, timestamp, path, requestId } }` |

For **RFC 7807** (`application/problem+json`) vs custom envelope, see `api-and-events.mdc` — pick one per API surface.

## Design defaults (when not specified)

- **Async** between services when requirements allow; justify synchronous calls.
- **OpenAPI-first** for new cross-service contracts.
- **DDD:** aggregates, value objects, repository ports in domain.
- **Resilience details:** `api-and-events.mdc`, `architecture-and-diagrams.mdc`.

## Documentation (when behavior or topology changes)

- `README.md` and `docs/agents-v0/diagrams/sequences/<service>.md` in the feature change
- `docs/agents-v0/architecture.md` and `docs/agents-v0/network.md`: `/v0-onboard` or the P0 build. Later, a docs-only follow-up

Authoritative refs (repo paths win if they differ): `docs/agents-v0/security-standards.md` + `security-baseline.mdc`; `docs/agents-v0/gold-standards.md`; `docs/agents-v0/quality-gates.md` / `docs/agents-v0/quality-quick-reference.md` + `quality-and-testing.mdc`.

## BFF and frontends

- **BFF:** aggregation, auth/session handoff, safe GET caching, rate limits, DTO mapping — **thin**; domain rules in domain services.
- Use **Spring MVC** or **WebFlux** per existing service — do not switch reactive/MVC without an architectural decision.
- **Frontend:** React default per `frontend-web.mdc`; API client, correlation + trace headers, 401 handling.

## OMS / order domain (when relevant)

Event-driven boundaries; sagas; idempotency keys on mutating ops; separate Order, Inventory, Payment, Fulfillment contexts — implement only when the task touches that domain. Details: `architecture-and-diagrams.mdc`.
